  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 257 AM EDT Fri May 8 2026\n\n- Northwest Flow Regime Continues\n\nUpper troughing across the Great Lakes will persist into next \nweek. Temperatures will run cooler than normal with Frost/Freeze \npotential or Saturday, Sunday and Monday nights. Clipper type lows\nwill occasionally bring showers in a northwest flow regime.\n\nA shortwave trough moves through tonight with scattered showers\ninto Saturday morning. The pattern repeats for Tuesday into\nTuesday night. The Tuesday low should have deeper moisture to \nwork with, but is moving fast enough to limit the chances of \nexcessive rainfall.",
